{"id":134363776662615,"type":"artist","name":"Lucinda Williams","artist":null,"year":1953,"weight":22,"info":{"tags":["singer-songwriter","Alt-country","country","female vocalists","americana"],"country":"US","begin":"1953-01-26","kind":"Person","similar":["Gillian Welch","Steve Earle","Mary Gauthier","Emmylou Harris","James McMurtry","Rosanne Cash","Patty Griffin","John Hiatt","Guy Clark","Steve Earle & The Dukes"],"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Lucinda_Williams_%26_guitar.jpg?width=500","bio":"Lucinda Williams (Lake Charles, Luisiana, 26 de enero de 1953) es una cantautora estadounidense de música rock, folk y country. Ha obtenido tres premios Grammy, y fue considerada la mejor autora de canciones de Estados Unidos por la revista TIME en 2002.\n\nWilliams, hija del poeta y profesor de literatura Miller Williams y de una pianista aficionada, Lucille Fern Day. Sus padres se divorciaron a mediados de la década de 1960. El padre de Williams obtuvo su custodia, la de su hermana, Karyn Elizabeth y su hermano menor, Robert Miller."},"works":[{"id":132386129776497,"type":"album","name":"Ramblin' on My Mind","artist":"Lucinda Williams","year":1979,"weight":9,"yt":"eOEVJKXaJoQ","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":14625077618763,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — American Folk Music","rank":175,"scaruffi":null},{"id":112872897412121,"name":"RYM Top — Blues — Acoustic Blues","rank":67,"scaruffi":null},{"id":119301033705212,"name":"RYM Top — Country — Progressive Country","rank":165,"scaruffi":null},{"id":132708326155004,"name":"RYM Top — Blues — Country Blues","rank":77,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":4}},{"id":31616570954573,"type":"album","name":"Happy Woman Blues","artist":"Lucinda Williams","year":1980,"weight":5,"yt":"q3zNUvMeFEA","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":119301033705212,"name":"RYM Top — Country — Progressive Country","rank":106,"scaruffi":null},{"id":228654689369664,"name":"RYM Top — Cou